  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through Monday)\nIssued at 258 AM EDT Tue Jun 23 2026\n\nThursday and Friday will likely see a return to afternoon \nconvection which will help moderate our peak temperatures. There's\nno strong signal for anything that might be severe, and by the \ntime the weekend comes we may see a lapse in convection as a \ntemporary ridge builds in. \n\nExpect highs in the upper 80s and lower 90s through the week, \nthough conditions will likely feel pretty muggy as SW flow \nprovides a near continuous stream of moisture out of the gulf. \nApparent temperatures could reach triple digits for parts of \ncentral Georgia on Friday and become more likely and more \nwidespread over the weekend.\n\nOvernight lows will likely remain muggy as well, with lows in the\nupper 60s and low 70s. Light and variable winds won't do us any \nfavors and do little in providing a relief from the heat that's \nexpected to build in.",
